      <div class="pp-two">
        <div class="pp-card">
          <h3>Important Laws</h3>
          <ul class="pp-list">
            <li><strong>KVL:</strong> Algebraic sum of voltages in a closed loop is zero.</li>
            <li><strong>KCL:</strong> Algebraic sum of currents at a node is zero.</li>
            <li><strong>Thevenin''s Theorem:</strong> A linear network seen from two terminals can be replaced by \(V_{TH}\) in series with \(R_{TH}\).</li>
            <li><strong>Shockley relation:</strong> \(I_D=I_{DSS}\left(1- rac{V_{GS}}{V_P}ight)^2\).</li>
            <li><strong>Maximum undistorted swing:</strong> Choose Q-point near the middle of active-region load line.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="pp-card">
          <h3>Most Important Derivations</h3>
          <ul class="pp-list">
            <li>DC load-line equation of diode circuit.</li>
            <li>Average DC and RMS output of half-wave and full-wave rectifiers.</li>
            <li>Alpha-beta relation of BJT.</li>
            <li>DC load line and Q-point for BJT.</li>
            <li>Voltage-divider bias equations.</li>
            <li>Hybrid parameter model of CE amplifier.</li>
            <li>JFET parameter relation \(\mu=g_mr_d\).</li>
            <li>Zener regulator design relation.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
