            <tr><td>Barrier potential</td><td>Potential developed across depletion region that opposes further diffusion of carriers.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>PIV</td><td>Maximum reverse voltage a diode can withstand without breakdown.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Ripple factor</td><td>Ratio of AC component RMS value to DC component in rectifier output.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Q-point</td><td>DC operating point of a transistor when no input signal is applied.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Thermal runaway</td><td>Self-increasing collector current caused by temperature rise in a transistor.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Coupling capacitor</td><td>Passes AC signal and blocks DC between amplifier stages.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Bypass capacitor</td><td>Provides low-reactance AC path around emitter or source resistance.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Transconductance</td><td>Change in output current per unit change in input control voltage.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Schottky diode</td><td>Metal-semiconductor diode with low forward voltage drop and fast switching.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Varactor diode</td><td>Reverse-biased diode used as voltage-controlled capacitance.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Seven-segment display</td><td>Display made from seven LED segments for decimal digits.</td></tr>
